# Performance Optimization Guidelines

## React Server Components
- Minimize 'use client', 'useEffect', and 'setState'; favor React Server Components (RSC)
- Use server components for data fetching when possible
- Only use client components when necessary for interactivity
- Follow the Next.js App Router architecture for optimal performance

## Component Optimization
- Wrap client components in Suspense with fallback
- Use dynamic loading for non-critical components
- Implement proper memoization with useMemo and useCallback
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders

## Image Optimization
- Optimize images with next/image
- Use WebP format for better compression
- Include size data (width and height) to prevent layout shifts
- Implement lazy loading for images below the fold

## JavaScript Optimization
- Minimize client-side JavaScript
- Implement proper code splitting with dynamic imports
- Use streaming where appropriate
- Optimize bundle size with tree shaking

## Caching and Data Fetching
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Use React Query or SWR for client-side data fetching
- Leverage Next.js caching mechanisms
- Implement incremental static regeneration when appropriate

## Core Web Vitals
- Optimize for Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)
- Minimize Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)
- Improve First Input Delay (FID) and Interaction to Next Paint (INP)
- Use the Web Vitals library to monitor performance 